IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpfta-types`
IMPORT `cpfta-part3b-offences`

-- Tests for Part 3B (ss 27 to 34).  Figures read off the text: a fine not exceeding
-- $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both (ss 27(1), 28, 29(3), 30);
-- composition up to the lower of one half of the maximum fine and $5,000 (s 34(1)).

§ `Tests -- Part 3B`

§§ `27 to 30. Penalties`

#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `an offence of failing to comply with a requirement (section 27)`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `an offence of failing to comply with a requirement (section 27)`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `an offence of destroying or falsifying documents (section 28)`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `an offence of giving false or misleading information (section 29)`)'s `the maximum term of imprisonment in months` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT (`the maximum penalty for the offence` `an offence of obstructing an officer of the Commission (section 30)`)'s `the maximum fine` EQUALS 10_000

§§ `27. Refusal to provide information, etc.`

-- Refusal Facts: fails to comply, requirement is to produce a document, document in the person's possession or control,
-- reasonably practicable to comply, requirement is to provide information or an explanation or say where a document is,
-- reasonable excuse, the person imposing the requirement failed to follow the section.
`refusing to produce a document that the person holds` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`failing to produce a document that is not held and could not practicably be got` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`failing to produce a document that is not held but could practicably be got` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`failing to produce a document that is held but could not practicably be produced` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`refusing information with no excuse` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`refusing information with a reasonable excuse` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a reasonable excuse offered for refusing to produce a document that is held` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`refusing a requirement the Commission imposed improperly` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`complying with the requirement` MEANS `Refusal Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `refusing to produce a document that the person holds`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `failing to produce a document that is not held and could not practicably be got`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `failing to produce a document that is not held but could practicably be got`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `failing to produce a document that is held but could not practicably be produced`
#ASSERT `the defence in section 27(2) is made out` `failing to produce a document that is not held and could not practicably be got`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `refusing information with no excuse`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `refusing information with a reasonable excuse`
#ASSERT `the defence in section 27(3) is made out` `refusing information with a reasonable excuse`
-- s 27(3) covers information, explanations and statements of where a document is; not production of a document
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `a reasonable excuse offered for refusing to produce a document that is held`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `refusing a requirement the Commission imposed improperly`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 27(1)` `complying with the requirement`

§§ `28. Destroying or falsifying documents`

-- Destruction Facts: required to produce a document, intentionally or recklessly destroys or falsifies, causes or permits it.
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 28` (`Destruction Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 28` (`Destruction Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 28` (`Destruction Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 28` (`Destruction Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)

§§ `29. False or misleading information`

-- False Information Facts: gives information to the Commission or its officers, gives it to another person knowing it will be
-- passed on, false or misleading in a material particular, knows, reckless.
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 29` (`False Information Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 29` (`False Information Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 29` (`False Information Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 29` (`False Information Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 29` (`False Information Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 29` (`False Information Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)

§§ `30. Obstructing officer of Commission, etc.`

-- Obstruction Facts: obstructs, hinders or impedes, in the discharge of duties or exercise of powers, reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 30` (`Obstruction Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 30` (`Obstruction Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 30` (`Obstruction Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 30` (`Obstruction Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)

§§ `31. No costs or damages or other relief arising from seizure`

-- Seizure Proceedings Facts: proceedings about a seized item, relief sought is return or payment of value, seizure without reasonable or probable cause.
#ASSERT `costs, damages or other relief is barred` (`Seizure Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `costs, damages or other relief is barred` (`Seizure Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `costs, damages or other relief is barred` (`Seizure Proceedings Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `costs, damages or other relief is barred` (`Seizure Proceedings Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `32 and 33. Offences by corporations, unincorporated associations and partnerships`

-- State of Mind Facts: it must be proved, by an officer, by an employee, by an agent (each within authority), that person had that state of mind.
#ASSERT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership` (`State of Mind Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership` (`State of Mind Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership` (`State of Mind Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- s 33(1) names an employee or agent, not an officer
#ASSERT NOT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `an unincorporated association` (`State of Mind Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `an unincorporated association` (`State of Mind Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `a partnership` (`State of Mind Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `a partnership` (`State of Mind Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the state of mind of the body is evidenced` `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership` (`State of Mind Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)

-- Body Offence Facts: kind of body, the body commits an offence, the person's role, consented or connived, knowingly concerned,
-- knew or ought to have known, failed to take all reasonable steps.
`an officer of a corporation who connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, TRUE, `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an officer of a corporation who knew and did nothing to stop it` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, TRUE, `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an officer of a corporation who knew but took every reasonable step` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, TRUE, `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`an officer of a corporation who neither knew nor connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, TRUE, `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a partner of an LLP who was knowingly concerned` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, TRUE, `a partner, or a person purporting to act as a partner`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a manager of a corporation who connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, TRUE, `an individual involved in the management of the body who is in a position to influence its conduct in relation to the commission of the offence`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a bystander who connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, TRUE, `none of those`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an officer of a corporation who connived, but the corporation committed no offence` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`, FALSE, `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a partner in a partnership who connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a partnership`, TRUE, `a partner, or a person purporting to act as a partner`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a committee member of an association who connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `an unincorporated association`, TRUE, `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a partner of an association who connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `an unincorporated association`, TRUE, `a partner, or a person purporting to act as a partner`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an officer of a partnership who connived` MEANS `Body Offence Facts` OF `a partnership`, TRUE, `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `an officer of a corporation who connived`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `an officer of a corporation who knew and did nothing to stop it`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `an officer of a corporation who knew but took every reasonable step`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `an officer of a corporation who neither knew nor connived`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `a partner of an LLP who was knowingly concerned`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `a manager of a corporation who connived`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `a bystander who connived`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `an officer of a corporation who connived, but the corporation committed no offence`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `a partner in a partnership who connived`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `a committee member of an association who connived`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `a partner of an association who connived`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of the same offence as the body` `an officer of a partnership who connived`

§§ `34. Composition of offences`

-- Composition Facts: prescribed as compoundable, compounder authorised, maximum fine, sum proposed, sum paid.
GIVEN maxfine IS A NUMBER
      sum IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Composition Facts`
`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` maxfine `compounded for` sum MEANS
    `Composition Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, maxfine, sum, FALSE

#ASSERT `the most that may be collected in composition` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 10_000 `compounded for` 0) EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected in composition` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 8_000 `compounded for` 0) EQUALS 4_000
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected in composition` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 20_000 `compounded for` 0) EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected in composition` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 10_002 `compounded for` 0) EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `the offence may be compounded for the sum proposed` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 10_000 `compounded for` 5_000)
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for the sum proposed` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 10_000 `compounded for` 5_001)
#ASSERT `the offence may be compounded for the sum proposed` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 8_000 `compounded for` 4_000)
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for the sum proposed` (`a compoundable offence with maximum fine` 8_000 `compounded for` 4_001)
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for the sum proposed` (`Composition Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, 10_000, 100, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for the sum proposed` (`Composition Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, 10_000, 100, FALSE)
#ASSERT `no further proceedings may be taken against the person in respect of the offence` (`Composition Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, 10_000, 100, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `no further proceedings may be taken against the person in respect of the offence` (`Composition Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, 10_000, 100, FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `no regulations under section 43(2)(n) prescribing compoundable offences are encoded in this model`
